// expect: 33
// band B M2 RATCHET — the UZero blast radius through call frames (pinned
// so M4's abandon cut is a MEASURED flip). Under today's convention the
// abort's None returns to the deepest perform site and reaches the install
// ONLY because every intermediate frame is a TAIL-position value chain
// (deep's recursive branch returns the recursion verbatim). A frame doing
// arithmetic on the result — `deep(n-1) + 1` — silently BREAKS the
// protocol (the None sentinel arithmetics into garbage; the enclosing
// Option match hits its exhaustive else): that is the blast radius M4's
// abandon semantics closes structurally.
//   TODAY: exit 33 (the None chains up three tail frames to the match).
//   M4: same exit by a different mechanism (the install delivers the
//   arm's None directly, no chain) — the pin survives the cut; only the
//   FRAGILITY (the non-tail break) disappears.
// The effect is this fixture's own (`Bail`), not the prelude's `Abort`: it
// pins an Option-returning op, and one namespace holds one `Abort`.
effect Bail {
  bail() -> Option(a)
}

handler my_catch {
  bail() => None
}

fn deep(n) with Bail = if n == 0 { bail() } else { deep(n - 1) }

fn main() = match (deep(3)) ~> my_catch {
  Some(v) => v,
  None    => 33
}
